# Source-derived semantics

- The source contains one instruction paragraph followed by one empty 200px by 200px div.
- The tested declaration is background: repeat-x bottom scroll green; and is preserved verbatim.
- Without an image, the required green fill proves whether the complete valid shorthand parsed; inert repeat/position/attachment tokens are intentionally retained.

# Compatibility adjustments

- Visible text uses wrapping outer text, nested bold text, and ordinary U+0020; the box selector is class-scoped.
- Content-box sizing and explicit body/paragraph spacing are setup-only Web compatibility adjustments.

# Current Lynx API-doc basis

- Background attachment is unsupported, so a stable missing green fill is an engine failure rather than grounds to rewrite or skip the assertion.
